{
  "public_post": "Important safety update: Yesterday's co‑op bread was made with a contaminated flour batch and may cause illness. If you purchased bread, please stop eating it, keep the loaf for a possible recall, and come to the co‑op for a full refund. We are arranging safe bread from the farm stand for today. If you feel unwell, seek medical care.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Initiate immediate recall of all unsold loaves and process refunds for yesterday's sales. Discard any remaining contaminated bread. Contact the flour supplier for a replacement batch; in the meantime, procure flour from the farm stand to resume baking tomorrow. Update the public board with recall details and refund process.",
  "reason": "Day 2 update to manage the contamination fallout, ensure safety, refunds, and plan alternative supply."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important notice: The flour batch used for this week's bread is contaminated, making all co‑op loaves unsafe. Please do NOT eat any co‑op bread, return any you have for a full refund, and we will resume baking only after safe flour is secured.",
  "coop_message": "All members: We must immediately recall all bread sold this week, issue refunds, and halt any further sales. Let's source safe flour (e.g., from the farm stand) or arrange a temporary supply, and prepare a clear public update for villagers explaining the recall and the temporary shortage.",
  "reason": "To protect residents from illness and coordinate the recall and alternative supply."
}

{
  "public_post": "Reminder: Do NOT eat any co‑op bread. We are recalling all loaves sold yesterday and will refund every resident. We are securing safe flour and aim to resume baking tomorrow. Thank you for your safety.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Initiate immediate recall of all bread sold on day 1 and process refunds for each resident. Contact the farm stand today to purchase emergency flour, arrange delivery, and plan to bake tomorrow with safe flour. Update the village on the recall status and expected resumption of service.",
  "reason": "To maintain public safety, manage the recall and refunds, and coordinate an urgent alternative flour source."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Lab results confirm the flour batch used this week is contaminated. All co‑op bread is unsafe and will be recalled. Refunds will be issued for any purchases made today. No bread will be sold until we secure safe flour, expected tomorrow.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Confirmed contamination. Issue refunds for today's sales and discard all loaves. Contact the farm stand to purchase flour for tomorrow's batch. Prepare a public notice for tomorrow confirming safe bread is back. Also discuss covering any extra costs from the stand.",
  "reason": "We need to inform villagers of the confirmed danger, handle refunds, and coordinate safe production for the rest of the week."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: All contaminated loaves have been recalled and refunds issued. Safe flour has been secured from the farm stand; we will resume baking safe bread today (Day 3). If you purchased bread on Day 1 or Day 2 and have not yet received a refund, please contact us. If you feel ill, seek medical care. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All refunds for Day 1 and Day 2 purchases have been processed. Safe flour from the farm stand has arrived; we will bake a fresh batch this morning for sale later today. Ensure the baking area is thoroughly sanitized, track inventory, and set prices. Discuss how to cover the extra cost of the farm‑stand flour from co‑op funds.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that safe bread is back and refunds are complete, and to coordinate final recall and resumption steps with co‑op members."
}

{
  "public_post": "Safe flour secured: co‑op bread will be back today. Refunds for all contaminated loaves have been issued; please collect yours at the shop. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All refunds for days 1‑2 are completed; ensure each resident receives theirs. We have safe flour from the farm stand and will bake 30 loaves today. Discuss covering the extra cost of the stand.",
  "reason": "To announce resumption of safe bread and coordinate refunds and production."
}

{
  "public_post": "Reminder: Any bread bought on Day 1 or Day 2 may still be unsafe – please bring it to the co‑op today for safe disposal (refunds have already been issued). Today's loaves are baked with safe flour and are available for purchase. If you experience any stomach issues, visit the clinic promptly.",
  "coop_message": "All members: We must finalize the accounting for the farm‑stand flour expense and decide on a temporary price adjustment to cover the extra cost; also confirm we have sufficient safe flour for the rest of the week and schedule a meeting with the village council to discuss reimbursement options.",
  "reason": "To ensure all remaining contaminated bread is removed, reassure villagers about safety, and address the co‑op’s financial shortfall from the emergency flour purchase."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: Safe flour has arrived and we are back baking today (Day 4). All refunds have been issued. Bread is available for purchase at the usual price; we appreciate your patience as we cover the extra cost of the emergency flour. If you feel ill, please visit the clinic.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we need to decide how to cover the extra cost of the farm‑stand flour used on days 3‑4. Options: use co‑op reserves, request a temporary modest price increase (e.g., 10 % extra), or seek village council assistance. Please vote by end of day.",
  "reason": "Update villagers on safe bread availability and coordinate the co‑op's financing of the emergency flour."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: safe flour has arrived and we are back to baking co‑op bread today (Day 4). All refunds for contaminated loaves have been issued. Today's loaves are safe to eat. We will resume normal sales; thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we have safe flour from the farm stand and will bake 30 loaves for Day 4. All refunds are complete. We need to decide how to cover the extra cost—suggest a modest temporary price increase or a village council subsidy. Please confirm pricing and inventory.",
  "reason": "Inform villagers that bread is safe and resume sales while coordinating cost coverage with the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: Safe flour secured and co‑op bread is back today (Day 4). All contaminated loaves have been recalled and refunds issued. Come by for fresh, safe bread. If you still have any suspect loaves, please bring them in for disposal.",
  "coop_message": "All refunds are completed; today we bake 30 loaves with safe flour. Let's track sales and inventory closely, and discuss how to cover the farm‑stand flour cost – propose a modest temporary price increase or seek council reimbursement. Also plan tomorrow’s supply.",
  "reason": "We need to tell villagers safe bread is available and coordinate cost‑covering measures with the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: Today's (Day 5) co‑op bread is safe and available. To cover the emergency farm‑stand flour cost, we are applying a modest temporary price increase of 10 % for the remainder of the week. Thank you for your understanding.",
  "coop_message": "Team, please finalize the accounting for the farm‑stand flour expense, confirm the 10 % temporary price increase and record votes by end of day, and ensure inventory for Day 5 and planning for Day 6.",
  "reason": "We need to inform villagers of safe bread and the price change, and coordinate the co‑op's accounting and pricing decision."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: Safe co‑op bread is available today (Day 5). To cover the emergency flour we purchased, we are applying a modest temporary price increase of 10 % (effective today) – this will be reviewed next week. Thank you for your continued support and patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we need to finalize how to cover the farm‑stand flour expense for Days 3‑5. Options: (1) use co‑op reserves, (2) implement a temporary 10 % price increase (as announced publicly), or (3) request a subsidy from the village council. Please cast your vote (A/B/C) by end of day so we can confirm the pricing and inform the village.",
  "reason": "Public post informs residents of safe bread and the temporary price change; coop message seeks a decision on cost coverage."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: Safe flour secured and co‑op bread is back today (Day 5). All loaves are safe to eat. We will continue baking and will update you soon about any temporary price adjustment to cover the emergency flour cost.",
  "coop_message": "We need to finalize how to cover the farm‑stand flour expense. I propose a modest temporary price increase of about 10 % for the remaining days (Day 5‑6), subject to village council approval. Please discuss and vote by end of day.",
  "reason": "Public post reassures villagers about safety and availability; co‑op message addresses the pending decision on covering extra flour costs."
}

{
  "public_post": "Final update: All contaminated loaves from Days 1‑2 have been recalled and refunds issued. Today's bread is safe and sold at the regular price. We thank you for your patience and will resume normal operations next week. If you experienced any illness, please let the clinic know.",
  "coop_message": "Team, close the books on the emergency: confirm all refunds processed, finalize the farm‑stand flour invoice, record the 10 % price increase applied on Days 5‑6 and plan to revert to standard pricing on Day 7; vote on whether to request council reimbursement for the extra flour cost (A: request subsidy, B: absorb from reserves).",
  "reason": "Provide a clear public closure of the incident and coordinate final accounting and reimbursement decisions within the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 6 update: All contaminated loaves have been fully recalled and refunds issued. The emergency flour cost has been covered by a modest temporary 10 % price increase, which will remain in effect until the village council reimburses the co‑op next week. Thank you for your patience and continued support – your health and the bakery’s sustainability remain our top priorities.",
  "coop_message": "Team, the vote is in: we’ll keep the 10 % temporary price increase to cover the farm‑stand flour expense. Accounting is finalized, and the extra revenue will be earmarked for reimbursement from the council. Thanks for handling the recall and keeping the bakery running safely. Let’s continue monitoring sales and health reports.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers of the final resolution and confirm the co‑op’s decision on covering the emergency flour cost."
}

{
  "public_post": "Final update (Day 6): Safe flour is secured and co‑op bread is back today. All refunds have been issued and any remaining suspect loaves should be returned for disposal. The temporary 10 % price increase will stay in effect through today and will be reviewed tomorrow; we appreciate your patience and continued support.",
  "coop_message": "Team, please finalize the accounting for the farm‑stand flour expense, confirm that the 10 % temporary price increase is applied for today, and prepare the report for the village council regarding reimbursement. Ensure inventory is closed out and all refund paperwork is archived. Vote now if anyone objects to the price increase; otherwise we’ll proceed with the current plan.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that bread is safe and the price increase remains, and to coordinate final accounting and council reporting within the co‑op."
}
